Cell["\<\
For hypergraph, each vertex is an index, and hyperedges are corresponding \
tensors. So in the above example, there are 3 tensors, labeled as 1, 2 and 3, \
with the first one having indices {1,2,3}, the second tensor with indices \
{2,1} and the third one with indices {4,3,2,5}\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.977579345520925*^9, 3.9775793842643003`*^9}, {
  3.977580693522562*^9, 
  3.9775807932476273`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"c4b89b79-7cde-4a47-893d-\
f0046ad7048d"],

